Had a wimpy ascension over the weekend:

No  Points     Name                                                   Hp [max]
 5    1344128  Codify-A ascended to demigod-hood.                    120 [120]

  Codify the Excavator       St:18/91 Dx:18 Co:18 In:17 Wi:18 Ch:13  Lawful
  Astral Plane $:28 HP:120(120) Pw:99(99) AC:10 Xp:15/268597 T:44186

No vampire/wraith tricks, there -- never was over 15th level.  My AC was
actually -10; I was naked when I grabbed this...  (I didn't find a
scroll of enchant armor in the whole game.  Weird.)

The tricky bit was the 120 hp -- it was touch and go on the astral plane
(what with visiting all three altars (what else is new?)), even with
conflict.  The wizard might have given me trouble if I hadn't moved so
fast; as it was I only met him twice (!).

My big break was a a wand of wishing with 3 initial charges (!!) which I
found just lying around way up on the 6th level or so.  Quickly I put it
to good use --

    Grayswandir
    gray dragon scale mail
    3 scrolls of charging
    shield of reflection
    bag of holding

and I held onto the last 2.  (Another argument for using all but the
last charge -- I lost the wand later.)  Speed boots and gauntlets of
power came from an armor shop.  (When I finally got to the castle I only
wished for a magic harp (for Medusa had imprisoned an Archon (who was
later christened Joe and eventually done in by a purple
worm...Burrrrp!)) and a spellbook of magic mapping.)

Down on the big level I pulled

    Stupid Hack Trick #23:

    	When you're running from a gelatinous cube and you want to
    	become unburdened, drop your bag of holding.

Slurp!  Idiot, me.  (Lost the wand of wishing there -- luckily the tool
shop in Minetown had another bag of holding.)  Oh, well.  *sheepish grin*

(With a bag of holding I actually like the idea that everything inside
was lost, but with a normal container it's probably a bug that the
non-organic contents go away instead of remaining in the beast.)

